{"game_id":2026020397,"away":"MTL","home":"COL","split":{"name":"Guhle","side":0,"sec":1762},"lede":"Colorado had last change, so Jared Bednar picked most of these matchups. Colorado played without Noah Juulsen. Montréal played without Brett Berard and lost Kaiden Guhle after 9:22 of the second.","notes":[{"kind":"match","head":"The third line drew Bolduc’s line","text":"Jared Bednar sent Schwartz, Svechkov and Hughes out for 6:09 of their 10:14 at 5-on-5 against Bolduc, Evans and Danault (60%, about 29% with no line matching), and the chances were close, 0.22 to 0.25 expected goals."},{"kind":"match","head":"Nečas’s line drew Suzuki’s line","text":"Lehkonen, Nelson and Nečas spent 6:56 of their 11:57 at 5-on-5 against Caufield, Suzuki and Slafkovský (58%, about 32% with no line matching), and they had the better of the chances, 1.03 to 0.28 expected goals. Colorado scored three of its six goals then."},{"kind":"exit","head":"After Guhle left, the lines changed","text":"Beck went from 15% to 26% and Danault from 24% to 32% of Montréal’s 5-on-5 time, and Slafkovský dropped from 32% to 21%. The matchups mostly stayed: the third line against Montréal’s third line (54% before, 68% after). One changed: Kadri’s line against Montréal’s second line (58% before, 24% after)."},{"kind":"result","head":"And it went better","text":"Montréal had 0.97 to 1.84 expected goals at 5-on-5 before Guhle left and 1.01 to 1.13 after. Montréal trailed for most of that stretch, though, and a team behind usually pushes the play, so the score explains part of it."}],"foot":"Jared Bednar matched about as hard as in his other home games: each line spent 48% of its time against one opposing line, against 32% to 50% in his last ten.","periods":{"all":{"0":{"rows":[{"label":"L1","names":["Caufield","Suzuki","Slafkovský"],"sec":776,"mixed":53,"vs":[416,73,162,125],"xgf":0.79,"xga":2.14,"gf":0,"ga":4,"cells":[[0.28,1.03,0,3],[0.01,0.19,0,0],[0.21,0.36,0,0],[0.17,0.48,0,1]]},{"label":"L2","names":["Ne